==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|la}} {{term|interrogatus}}, past participle of {{term|interrogare||to ask, question}} < {{term|inter||between}} + {{term|rogare||to ask}}; see [[rogation]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-interrogate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|interrogat|ed}}

# {{transitive}} To [[question]] or [[quiz]], especially in a [[thorough]] or [[aggressive]] manner.
#: ''The police '''interrogated''' the suspect at some length before they let him go.''

